{{!
    @template local_dimensions/central/tab_hash

    Names the tab core/dynamic_tabs should open, before it initialises.

    core/dynamic_tabs opens the FIRST tab in the DOM and ignores the server's active flag -
    its allActiveTabs selector matches every enabled tab link and takes the first. The one
    lever that overrides that is the URL fragment, which its openTabFromHash reads from
    document.location at init time. So the saved tab has to be in the fragment before that
    runs, and it has to get there synchronously: an AMD module cannot, because the plugin's
    own context module demonstrably initialises after core has already opened and fetched a
    tab. Core's own dynamic_tabs template uses a bare script tag for the same reason and
    says so - "We must not use the JS helper otherwise this gets executed too late".

    Render this immediately BEFORE the core/dynamic_tabs template.

    history.replaceState rather than assigning location.hash: assigning would scroll the
    page to the tab pane, whose id is the same shortname, and would push a history entry.
    An fragment the visitor typed themselves is left alone.

    The value is one of frankenstyle-free shortnames frameworks, structure or plans,
    allowlisted server-side in central.php before it reaches this template.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * activetab string Shortname of the tab to open.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "activetab": "plans"
    }
}}
<script>
    (function() {
        if (!document.location.hash) {
            window.history.replaceState(null, '', document.location.pathname
                + document.location.search + '#{{activetab}}');
        }
    })();
</script>
